    <string name="bmi_infant_guidance">Under 2 years\nBMI-for-age classification is not recommended in this calculator. Infants should be assessed using WHO growth standards, including weight-for-length, with a healthcare professional. No adult category or weight target is shown.</string>
    <string name="bmi_child_guidance">Children and teens, ages 2–19\nCDC BMI-for-age categories depend on age in months and sex used by the growth reference. The BMI number alone cannot be compared with adult cutoffs. The reference range is not a weight-loss target; growth and health need professional assessment.</string>
    <string name="bmi_adult_guidance">Adults, ages 20 and over\nCDC adult cutoffs apply regardless of age or sex. BMI is a screening measure, not a diagnosis, and does not distinguish muscle from fat. Older adults need interpretation alongside muscle mass, nutrition and overall health. Pregnancy requires different assessment.</string>
